WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160 line:88%
Speech production and language are different assessment targets.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.110 line:88%
Speech involves the sounds and patterns used to say

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:06.810 line:88%
a message.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.570 line:88%
Historical descriptions of mild to moderate hearing loss emphasize

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.050 line:88%
single consonant and blend errors, especially affricates and fricatives.

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.790 line:88%
More severe early hearing loss without early auditory access

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.770 line:88%
can affect several speech systems.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.730 line:88%
The lecture's severe to profound profile is variable, and

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.230 line:88%
the instructor qualifies it by the history of early

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:26.930 line:88%
access.

00:00:27.585 --> 00:00:29.390 line:88%
It is not an outcome to assign to every

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.670 line:88%
child with that audiogram.

00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:34.877 line:88%
Intelligibility asks how much a listener understands.

00:00:35.672 --> 00:00:37.927 line:88%
In a recorded sample, the listener can write the

00:00:37.927 --> 00:00:41.327 line:88%
words heard, and the examiner calculates the percentage identified

00:00:41.327 --> 00:00:42.027 line:88%
correctly.

00:00:42.857 --> 00:00:45.827 line:88%
In this illustrated example, fifteen of twenty words are

00:00:45.827 --> 00:00:49.387 line:88%
recognized: seventy-five percent intelligibility.

00:00:50.187 --> 00:00:53.467 line:88%
The denominator is words in the sample, not consonants

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.167 line:88%
attempted.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:58.087 line:88%
Another method asks listeners to rate the recognizability of

00:00:58.087 --> 00:00:58.827 line:88%
the whole passage.

00:00:59.627 --> 00:01:04.627 line:88%
An articulation test identifies specific sound errors; intelligibility describes

00:01:04.627 --> 00:01:06.327 line:88%
how well the message gets through.
